[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58082,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma is an exceptionally rare, aggressive adipocytic neoplasm, typically occurring in children and adolescents. Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma shows mixed histological features of conventional myxoid liposarcoma and pleomorphic liposarcoma and lacks the gene fusions and amplifications of myxoid liposarcoma, atypical lipomatous tumour, and dedifferentiated liposarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58083,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8859/3 Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T18:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58084,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>2B59.Y &amp; XH3EL0 &amp; XH25R1 Liposarcoma, other specified primary site &amp; Myxoid liposarcoma &amp; Pleomorphic liposarcoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T15:28:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58085,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> pleomorphic myxoid liposarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58086,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58087,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma has a predilection for the mediastinum {19194281; 22420730; 22895273}. Other reported locations include the thigh, head and neck, perineum, abdomen, and back {19194281; 24970901; 26647907; 28160093}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58088,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma generally manifests as a large, deep-seated soft tissue mass {24970901; 26647907}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58089,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma occurs predominantly in children and young adults. Patient age in the large majority of published cases is &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;years {19194281; 24970901; 26647907; 28160093}. There is a female predominance {19194281}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58090,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58091,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma has been associated with Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome {28160093}, numerical chromosomal aberrations, and inactivation of the <em>RB1</em> tumour suppressor gene {26647907; 30853315; 30852046; 30850231; 30857767}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58092,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, myxoid pleomorphic liposarcomas are non-encapsulated tumours with ill-defined margins {24970901}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58093,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histologically, the tumours show variable proportions of myxoid liposarcoma&ndash;like areas, characterized by abundant myxoid matrix, scattered lipoblasts, relatively bland primitive round to oval cells, and a delicate curvilinear to plexiform capillary network {19194281; 24970901}. Lymphangioma-like myxoid pools can be observed {24970901}. Pleomorphic spindle or ovoid cells with hyperchromatic nuclei may be scattered within the myxoid component, with a progressive transition into more-cellular, high-grade pleomorphic liposarcoma&ndash;like areas displaying severe cytological atypia, increased mitotic activity, atypical mitoses, pleomorphic lipoblasts, and occasional necrosis {19194281; 24970901}. Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcomas have a nonspecific immunophenotype.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58094,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58095,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FISH studies have shown that myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma lacks the <em>FUS</em>/<em>EWSR1</em>-<em>DDIT3</em> gene fusions seen in conventional myxoid liposarcoma, as well as the <em>MDM2</em> amplification present in well-differentiated/dedifferentiated liposarcoma {19194281; 24970901}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58096,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> distinctive admixture of relatively bland zones resembling conventional myxoid liposarcoma and much more cellular and atypical areas, resembling pleomorphic liposarcoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable (in selected cases):</em> absence of <em>FUS</em>/<em>EWSR1</em>-<em>DDIT3</em> gene fusions and <em>MDM2</em> amplifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58097,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM systems can be applied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58098,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 250,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoid pleomorphic liposarcoma is an extremely aggressive tumour type with a high recurrence rate; metastasis to lung, bone, and soft tissue; and poor overall survival {19194281; 22420730}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:10:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]